(docs/BUGS_FOUND.md #130: the field type check refuses only a value of
 another type. A value of the field's own type, a converted one, another
 field of the same type, and a time into a time field are all written.)

A thing called measurement has
  a number called count is 0,
  a float called level is 0.0,
  a boolean called ready is false,
  a time called taken,
  a text called label is "12".

a measurement called sample.
a measurement called duplicate.
Set sample's count to sample's label as a number.
Set sample's level to sample's count as a float.
Set sample's ready to true.
a time called now is current time.
Set sample's taken to now.
Set duplicate's count to sample's count.
Print sample's count.
Print sample's level.
If sample's ready then, print "ready".
Print duplicate's count.
If sample's taken is now then, print "the time is kept".
